#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:5
#: ad7a5d4333304741b18098cee4cab3b5
msgid "C.H.U.C.K Autopilot (for Parrot Disco)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:7
#: b6aa0b33792c4543985471a36dc83016
msgid "The heart of the Parrot Disco is the C.H.U.C.K autopilot, an orange box which is a general purpose autopilot. It is perfectly possible to use the C.H.U.C.K in a different airframe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:11
#: 165bf13ab23f41c580e4eb2a65586bea
msgid "To use the C.H.U.C.K outside of a Disco the first thing you will notice is it has 7 servo/motor outputs available. There are 6 PWM 3-pin servo connectors, and one connector from the I2C ESC that can be used to drive a brushless motor (it drives the motor on the Disco)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:16
#: 4013775942bf4f71ac94b6434df80c8d
msgid "The mapping between ArduPilot output channel numbers and the 7 outputs was chosen with ease of integration with the Disco in mind, which resulted in a fairly strange pin ordering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:20
#: f68d08847ae74dd6a8519f91996db676
msgid "Servo rail pin numbers in the list below are from left to right when looking at the C.H.U.C.K from the back, so pin1 on the servo rail is closest to the first 'C' in 'C.H.U.C.K' on the case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:24
#: 593bdc77d653467ab607e2465f687d16
msgid "channel 1 : servo rail pin 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:25
#: 1caa8d43725e4b43b7c00909ad0e568e
msgid "channel 2 : servo rail pin 6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:26
#: 8f7f4a8019944ca1a174ad3aeb9c0504
msgid "channel 3 : I2C ESC motor output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:27
#: ebacda56b5b14acea6019a78335d9d5a
msgid "channel 4 : servo rail pin 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:28
#: 9f562da3e5d04c4cb18bbc4e38a08321
msgid "channel 5 : servo rail pin 5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:29
#: 9f68140f86b3498eb893359cb8b6c93b
msgid "channel 6 : servo rail pin 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:30
#: 72655b07096844b5b28bfaf930486c50
msgid "channel 7 : servo rail pin 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:32
#: b9ab03c46afc456cb1999756716c88b9
msgid "Note that this pin ordering means you will need some extra parameter settings if you are not using the I2C ESC motor controller for throttle output. To take the simple example of a 4 channel fixed wing plane (aileron, elevator, throttle, rudder) you could configure and wire it like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:38
#: d68d4f00f5be4d06900843f9ea8d4388
msgid "servo rail pin1 : ailerons (on Y-lead if need be for 2 servos)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:39
#: fd4e3443ea17435881017903488f3b59
msgid "servo rail pin6 : elevator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:40
#: de65b953ec0b4c83a0c21376140de83d
msgid "servo rail pin5 : throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:41
#: 81317279c54a45a2bb80f1cf45d16824
msgid "servo rail pin2 : rudder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:42
#: e0bada3ece7046bea0a95a39ad5cbf1f
msgid "set SERVO5_FUNCTION=70 or RC5_FUNCTION=70 to make channel 5 output throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:43
#: 995bcb9aa668488b81baca42b63f0a8f
msgid "set SERVO5_MIN/RC5_MIN, SERVO5_MAX/RC5_MAX and SERVO5_TRIM/RC5_TRIM for the throttle range of your motor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:45
#: 3e924627e8dd493e9fb865b7d3935fb5
msgid "Apart from that pin mapping, setting up a C.H.U.C.K with another airframe is the same as with any aircraft with ArduPilot. It could be used with any vehicle type supported by ArduPilot, including gliders, quadplanes, petrol planes, multicopters or rovers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:50
#: 2d30fe1f3fb04db4a0d9c556a8d01f7e
msgid "For R/C input there is a 3-pin servo lead connector on the left side of the C.H.U.C.K which accepts the following widely used R/C protocols:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:54
#: d187f2d65c66465690da754cb83e8fe2
msgid "SBUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:55
#: fa3cad02fe9a40529dbf5f644f670a6c
msgid "DSM/Skektrum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:56
#: 7ab9ab762a3d4f5a958376916e800ebd
msgid "SUMD (Graupner)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:57
#: c9dec1faba63435aa6ebcf6711a25b5a
msgid "ST24 (Yuneec)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-CHUCK-overview.rst:59
#: 7d6f877eb90e4d7ea675cf1a7023580a
msgid "The use of the airspeed sensor and sonar will be dependent on the physical shape of the airframe and whether the positioning of these sensors is suitable for the layout of the C.H.U.C.K."
msgstr ""
